<title>UK: Amstrad to suspend shares ahead of hearing.</title>
<headline>Amstrad to suspend shares ahead of hearing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>British consumer electronics firm Amstrad Plc said on Friday its shares would be suspended from July 29 in anticipation of a court hearing on its restructuring.</p>
<p>The company said the hearing to approve the reorganisation would be held on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Under the reorganisation, Amstrad would change its name to Viglen Technology Plc, which was expected to begin trading under the new name on August 4.</p>
<p>Amstrad's shares ended down 4.5p to 275 on Friday. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
